      {
        "question_text": "A shop had $235$ seed packets. It received $148$ more, then sold $97$.\n(a) How many packets were left?\n(b) The next day it sold $64$ packets and received $39$ more. How many packets did it have then?",
        "solution_text": "(a) Combine the packets, then subtract those sold.\n$235+148=383$\n$383-97=286$\nThere were $286$ packets left.\n(b) Start with the result from (a).\n$286-64=222$\n$222+39=261$\nThere were $261$ packets.\nCheck (a): $240+150-100=290$. The exact answer $286$ is close to this estimate."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A traveller went $175$ km by train, $68$ km by bus and $12$ km on foot. What was the total distance travelled?",
        "solution_text": "Add the train and bus distances, then add the walking distance.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}175+68\\\\&=243\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}243+12\\\\&=255\\end{aligned}$\nThe total distance travelled was $255$ km."
      }
    ],
